Subject: lazy JSON.parse and JSON construction fast paths

Technical overview
  Adds lazy JSON.parse for large documents using one shared source,
  structural tape, immediate tape-node markers, direct scalar/container
  materialization, repeated-layout construction and access feedback. Eager
  JSON parsing uses direct key-to-atom scanning and owned dense-array transfer
  for the numeric-array fast path.

  Lazy parsing is enabled by default for large documents and can be disabled
  per runtime with JS_SetJSONLazyEnabled() or overridden for testing with
  QJS_JSON_LAZY=0/1. Lazy containers retain the document through a private
  non-enumerable property; unsupported values use the existing fallback parser.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

